re (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Maryland's 2026 governor's race is a rematch of 2022, with Democratic incumbent Wes Moore seeking a second term against Republican Dan Cox. Moore enters with a 56% approval rating in a state that leans Democratic by about 15 points, and he has raised more than $15 million to Cox's roughly $240,000. The only recent poll, from early August, showed Moore ahead 58% to 31%.\n\nEvery major race rater calls the contest Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets give Moore a 97% to 98% chance of winning. Cox secured his party's nomination in June but has run a low-profile campaign with minimal resources. The evidence points to a comfortable Moore win, with the main open question being the size of the margin rather than the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 19.52}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9967, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9939, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9968, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9959, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9942, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9961, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9947, "margin": 20.5}]}